From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: notify watchers of both sides of a rename

Purpose: keep folder views and shell clients notified when an item is renamed into a watched folder.
XP behavior: the shell change-notify service matches registrations against both PIDLs for two-item events (shell32/scnotify.cpp, CChangeNotify::_AddToClients).
Wine before: the two-item path branch checked only the old PIDL; its second-PIDL branch was unreachable. New-delivery notifications also copied the aligned second PIDL into shared memory sized without the alignment padding.
Change: match rename notifications against both PIDLs and allocate shared memory for the aligned payload.
Evidence: XP source at Source/XPSP1/NT/shell/shell32/scnotify.cpp calls _MatchAndNotify for pidl and pidlExtra.
Scope: all processes.
---
dlls/shell32/changenotify.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/shell32/changenotify.c b/dlls/shell32/changenotify.c
--- a/dlls/shell32/changenotify.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/changenotify.c
@@ -349,10 +349,11 @@
                     notify = TRUE;
                 else if( wEventId & SHCNE_NOITEMEVENTS )
                     notify = TRUE;
-                else if( wEventId & ( SHCNE_ONEITEMEVENTS | SHCNE_TWOITEMEVENTS ) )
+                else if( wEventId & SHCNE_ONEITEMEVENTS )
                     notify = should_notify( Pidls[0], pidl, subtree );
                 else if( wEventId & SHCNE_TWOITEMEVENTS )
-                    notify = should_notify( Pidls[1], pidl, subtree );
+                    notify = should_notify( Pidls[0], pidl, subtree ) ||
+                             should_notify( Pidls[1], pidl, subtree );
             }
         }
 
@@ -395,7 +396,7 @@
                         memcpy(notification->data+offset, Pidls[1], size2);
 
                     shared_data = SHAllocShared(notification,
-                        sizeof(struct new_delivery_notification)+size1+size2,
+                        sizeof(struct new_delivery_notification)+offset+size2,
                         GetCurrentProcessId());
                     SHFree(notification);
                 }
